[ti:Glass Orchards]
[ar:Fern & Static]
[al:Small Weather]
[by:Vela demo — original lyrics]

[00:07.74]Glass orchards on the county line
[00:11.61]Every branch a little wire
[00:15.48]We drove out past the last streetlight
[00:19.35]Just to watch the sky catch fire
[00:23.23]You had a tape of songs you loved
[00:27.10]I had a map I couldn't read
[00:30.97]The heater hummed, the windows fogged
[00:34.84]And that was everything we'd need
[00:38.71]Oh, the orchards ring like bottles
[00:42.58]When the wind comes through the rows
[00:46.45]Oh, we're only glass and shadow
[00:50.32]And the light goes where it goes
[00:54.19]Somebody's porch light left on late
[00:58.06]A dog that barks at nothing much
[01:01.94]The whole town sleeping through the ache
[01:05.81]Of wanting something we can't touch
[01:09.68]Oh, the orchards ring like bottles
[01:13.55]When the wind comes through the rows
[01:17.42]Oh, we're only glass and shadow
[01:21.29]And the light goes where it goes
